complaining of back pain that started suddenly
after one hour of gardening. Her past medical
history is unremarkable. She has been healthy
and active until the event. She does not smoke
and drinks alcohol in moderation. On
examination, the lumbar spine''s flexion,
extension, and rotation are significantly limited,
and tenderness between L4 and L5 is elicited.
There is no tenderness over the vertebral
bodies. After prescribing analgesics, which of
the following would be the most appropriate
next step in management?','{"A":"Bed rest.","B":"Referral for orthopedic consultation.\nfe Use of corsets.","C":"Advise that she should maintain","D":"physical activity.","E":"Magnetic resonance imaging of the\nlumbar spine."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-749105d25ba5","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"83a234601ca528b907e8","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_page":106,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"83a234601ca528b907e8","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":106,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Orthopaedics/Rheumatology","stem":"A 58-year-old woman presents to your GP clinic\ncomplaining of back pain that started suddenly\nafter one hour of gardening. Her past medical\nhistory is unremarkable. She has been healthy\nand active until the event. She does not smoke\nand drinks alcohol in moderation. On\nexamination, the lumbar spine''s flexion,\nextension, and rotation are significantly limited,\nand tenderness between L4 and L5 is elicited.\nThere is no tenderness over the vertebral\nbodies. After prescribing analgesics, which of\nthe following would be the most appropriate\nnext step in management?","options":{"A":"Bed rest.","B":"Referral for orthopedic consultation.\nfe Use of corsets.","C":"Advise that she should maintain","D":"physical activity.","E":"Magnetic resonance imaging of the\nlumbar spine."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"s