Department for an ongoing central chest pain
that started about 1 hour ago. He has the
history of recurrent chest pains that are
brought on with exertion and relieved with
rest, and type II diabetes mellitus. Further
assessment establishes the diagnosis of
unstable angina. You start him on aspirin,
clopidogrel, heparin, and glyceryl trinitrate.
The on-call cardiologist advises that you start
him on tirofiban as well if it is not
contraindicated. Which one of the following
is not a contraindication for tirofiban?','{"A":"Non-ST elevation myocardial\ninfarction (NSTEMI).","B":"Acute pericarditis.","C":"Vasculitis.","D":"Aortic dissection.","E":"History of intracranial neoplasm.\n\n—_— . a"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Pharmacology 1-33.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-d54cc8aaf70c","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"175b344bd45957eb184c","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Pharmacology 1-33.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Pharmacology 1-33.pdf","source_page":1,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"1e5ebff8933d2569fb10","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex Pharma Onco Immuno 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex Pharma Onco Immuno 2025.pdf","source_page":53,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"afc3dfcf3967256b391b","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1444,"source_qid":"232"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"175b344bd45957eb184c","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Pharmacology 1-33.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Pharmacology 1-33.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":1,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Pharmacology","stem":"A 70-year-old man presents to the Emergency\nDepartment for an ongoing central chest pain\nthat started about 1 hour ago. He has the\nhistory of recurrent chest pains that are\nbrought on with exertion and relieved with\nrest, and type II diabetes mellitus. Further\nassessment establishes the diagnosis of\nunstable angina. You start him on aspirin,\nclopidogrel, heparin, and glyceryl trinitrate.\nThe on-call ca