A 56-year-old man is admitted to the hospital
for treatment of methicillin resistant
Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA) pneumonia.
He is a Known case of hypertension and on
amilodipine and hydrochlorothiazide. You
decide to start him on vancomycin. Twenty
minutes after intravenous infusion of
vancomycin is started, he develops a
generalized erythematous rash all over his
body. There is no respiratory symptom and
the vitals are within the normal range. Which
one of the following is the most likely cause
of this presentation?','{"A":"Idiosyncratic drug reaction.","B":"Toxic shock syndrome.","C":"Stevens-Johnson syndrome.","D":"Anaphylaxis.","E":"Fixed drug eruption."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Pharmacology 1-33.pdf","supporting_pages":[68],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-0c9e6d5a0e27","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"356a6f751266dac3520b","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Pharmacology 1-33.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Pharmacology 1-33.pdf","source_page":68,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"356a6f751266dac3520b","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Pharmacology 1-33.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Pharmacology 1-33.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":68,"supporting_pages":[68],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Pharmacology","stem":"OMt JIZe:\nA 56-year-old man is admitted to the hospital\nfor treatment of methicillin resistant\nStaphylococcus aureus (MRSA) pneumonia.\nHe is a Known case of hypertension and on\namilodipine and hydrochlorothiazide. You\ndecide to start him on vancomycin. Twenty\nminutes after intravenous infusion of\nvancomycin is started, he develops a\ngeneralized erythematous rash all over his\nbody. There is no respiratory symptom and\nthe vitals are within the normal range. Which\none of the following is the most likely cause\nof this presentation?","options":{"A":"Idiosyncratic drug reaction.","B":"Toxic shock syndrome.","C":"Stevens-Johnson syndrome.","D":"Anaphylaxis.","E":"Fixed drug eruption."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence"